worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_wikipedia_and_shell_commands.js"
  ceiling 1392
  rationale "Definition merging, entity-name correction and who-is questions, terminal command detection, and the Wikipedia search, summary and disambiguation lookup. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 1285 to 1318 with the entity-grounded hours place lookup and its seed cache. Ceiling moved 1318 to 1387 with issue #1175's NATURAL_LANGUAGE_MARKER_WORDS guard (parsesAsCommandArguments and maskQuotedSpans mirroring src/solver_terminal.rs), so a prompt like 'Find the bug: def average(xs): ...' is a debugging request, not a shell command. Ceiling moved 1387 to 1389 with issue #1166 R1166-8: leadingShellCommand consults obligationCarriesWork, as leading_shell_command consults request_carries_work_obligations, so a sentence about building something is not a shell command. Ceiling moved 1389 to 1392 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds."
